+## New: “complete” AWS module (EKS + IRSA + RDS + Vault)
+Folder: `terraform/aws/eks`
+
+This module provisions:
+- minimal EKS cluster
+- S3 bucket + lifecycle
+- RDS Postgres (public for simplicity)
+- IRSA role for `aegis-model-serving`
+- Vault via Helm (dev mode + injector enabled) for token file at `/vault/secrets/token`
+
+⚠️ Production notes:
+- Replace public subnet / public RDS with private networking and proper node groups.
+- Replace Vault dev mode with HA storage backend.
+
+## OpenAI surface area
+- `/v1/openai/models`
+- `/v1/openai/chat/completions`
+- `/v1/openai/embeddings` (proxy to vLLM embeddings route if supported)
+- `/v1/openai/responses` (translated to chat completions)
+
+## Streaming token metering
+Streaming now meters tokens by parsing OpenAI-style SSE deltas and tokenizing via `tiktoken` (fallback heuristic).
+Env:
+- `AEGIS_TOKENIZER=tiktoken|heuristic`
+- `AEGIS_TIKTOKEN_ENCODING=cl100k_base`
+
+## Job workload identity for callbacks
+Callbacks can be authorized without shared HMAC if the caller is a workload identity:
+- claim `workload=true` (configurable)
+- role includes `aegis_job` (configurable)
+When workload identity is used, `AEGIS_REQUIRE_CALLBACK_SIGNATURE` can remain true for humans, but workloads bypass HMAC.
